L - List a file, with word wrap, and carriage return after every line(Useful when reading Stylo documents, and other Long Line files)Usage: l [-options] [file] [file] [-options]    -no  = width (default 79, max 256)     file = list of files to be listed    -f   = form feed after each file     -l   = end line at line feed     -t=n = tab-stop every 'n' characters (default = 4)    -z=xx= read filenames from xx (default = stdin)    -?   = report help L will treat any unrecognised characters less than hex 20 as a space.This includes optionally tab, and Line Feed.The listing is sent to std output.If no files are specified on the command line, then the program will read and output std input.